%S A392517 0,2,5,8,12,16,20,25,30,35,40,46,52,58,64,70,77,84,91,98,105,112,120,
%T A392517 128,136,144,152,160,168,177,186,195,204,213,222,231,240,250,260,270,
%U A392517 280,290,300,310,320,330,341,352,363,374,385,396,407,418,429,440,452,464,476,488
%N A392517 a(n) is the minimum diameter of a n-element set of integers for which no nonzero d has more than d-1 representations as a difference of elements of the set.
%C A392517 a(n+1) - a(n) follows A003057. This was first observed empirically and was proved by Ariel Williams (2026), whose explicit rulers attain the greedy lower bound of Gupta and O'Bryant for every n. - _John Akwei_, Nov 20 2026
%H A392517 John Akwei, <a href="/A392517/b392517.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A392517 John Akwei, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24369830">The threshold g_0(b) for g-Golomb rulers via padded LM rulers</a>, Zenodo, 2026. See Corollary 4.
%H A392517 Aditya A. Gupta, <a href="https://github.com/Dirac3011/lambda-sets/tree/main">Code for generating Linear Multiplicity Rulers</a>.
%H A392517 Aditya Gupta, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.14229">Optimal Diameters of High Multiplicity g-Golomb Rulers</a>, arXiv:2605.14229 [math.CO], 2026. See p. 2.
%H A392517 Ariel Williams, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24259347">The sharp asymptotic diameter of linear-multiplicity rulers</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A392517 Ariel Williams, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24362078">Closing the Gaps with the AW Schedules: The Exact Minimum Diameter of Linear-Multiplicity Rulers</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A392517 (8/9)^0.5*(n-1)^1.5 <= a(n) <= 1.75*((n+1)^1.5-(n+1)).
%F A392517 From _John Akwei_, Nov 20 2026: (Start)
%F A392517 a(n) = (k^3 - k)/3 + (k+1)*(n - 1 - k*(k-1)/2), where k = floor((1 + sqrt(8*n-7))/2) (Williams).
%F A392517 a(n) = Sum_{j=2..n} A003057(j).
%F A392517 a(n) = (2*sqrt(2)/3)*n^(3/2) + n + O(n^(1/2)). (End)
%e A392517 a(10)=[0, 2, 5, 8, 12, 16, 20, 25, 30, 35].
%e A392517 a(11)=[0, 2, 6, 9, 12, 16, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40].
%e A392517 a(12)=[0, 2, 6, 9, 12, 16, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40, 46].
